imagecodecs — pruned WASM build (Pyodide/Emscripten)
=====================================================

`imagecodecs-2026.6.26-cp312-abi3-pyodide_2025_0_wasm32.whl` is a custom build of
Christoph Gohlke's `imagecodecs` (https://github.com/cgohlke/imagecodecs), cross-compiled
for Pyodide's wasm32/Emscripten target rather than the upstream project's own manylinux/
macOS/Windows wheels. It is not published to PyPI — there is no wasm build there — which
is why it ships in this repo and is installed by URL rather than by name.

Pruned on purpose
------------------
Only the compiled extensions needed to decode the compression schemes tifffile actually
encounters day to day are included, to keep the wheel small for a browser download:

- `_shared` — common codec plumbing
- `_imcd`   — the core IMCD library: LZW, PackBits, Delta, floating-point predictor,
              bitorder reversal, and friends (most non-JPEG TIFF compression lives here)
- `_zlib`   — Deflate/zlib (TIFF compression 8/32946)
- `_jpeg8`  — baseline JPEG (TIFF compression 7)
- `_zstd`   — Zstandard (TIFF compression 50000)
- `_blosc`  — Blosc (used by some Zarr-backed formats, not TIFF)

Codecs outside that list (WebP, JPEG 2000, JPEG XL, LERC, HEIF/AVIF, PNG, ...) are absent.
`imagecodecs` itself tolerates this by design: each codec's compiled extension is
imported independently, and calling one whose `.so` isn't present raises
`DelayedImportError` at call time rather than failing the whole package import — so a
TIFF using an unlisted compression will still fail, but with a codec-specific error
instead of taking `tifffile` down for every TIFF.

Provenance / integrity
-----------------------
Rebuild by cross-compiling `imagecodecs` 2026.6.26 for Pyodide's wasm32 target with only
the above extensions enabled; see the upstream project's own build docs for the Pyodide
toolchain. `LICENSE` here is the upstream BSD-3-Clause licence, copied unmodified from
the wheel's own `dist-info/licenses/LICENSE`.

The platform tag in the filename and in `dist-info/WHEEL` (`pyodide_2025_0_wasm32`) must
match the `abi_version` micropip reads off the running Pyodide (`pyodide-lock.json` at
whatever `PYODIDE_VERSION` `kernel.js` pins — currently 0.28.0, whose lock reports
`abi_version: "2025_0"`). micropip parses that tag into an Emscripten version and rejects
the wheel outright, before looking at its contents, if it doesn't match — a wheel that
shipped here once tagged `pyemscripten_2026_0_wasm32` failed this way. Rebuilding for a
newer Pyodide means re-tagging (and re-testing) against that Pyodide's own lockfile, not
just bumping the year.

Why it's here instead of on the Pyodide CDN
--------------------------------------------
`tifffile` (installed on demand by `kernel.js`/`scratch-worker.js`, see `CLAUDE.md`) is
pure Python and works without `imagecodecs`, but silently can't decode any TIFF that uses
LZW, Deflate, JPEG, or Zstd compression — which is most real microscopy TIFFs — and
raises deep inside `tifffile` rather than at the point a cell touches the file. Installing
this wheel alongside `tifffile` closes that gap.
